FerrionOS change to base (MIT license, kept), made against upstream commit 20f7573b4dc011ea5267189185edc0b2f12bab0f, applied after ferrion-lockdown.patch (security roadmap S13):
- lived serves a second disk, /scheme/disk.live/1: the boot image as the bootloader loaded it, read-only (writes fail with EROFS; the disk scheme has no truncation), and open to root only like /scheme/disk.live/0.
- it reads the loaded image itself, which the live session never writes (its writes go to disk 0's overlay), so it is not a copy of a mounted filesystem: a clone of it is the unmodified boot image, consistent, without anything the live session wrote.
- the installer's fast install clones it, since the live root filesystem holds disk 0's only handle and physical memory is open to drivers only.

